/-!
# Candidate-A zero modes generated by Noether identities

The augmented Candidate-A quadratic action is the genuine same-action Hessian
on the unique D10-free Hilbert completion.  A physical symmetry direction
should therefore enter the kernel through its action-level first-variation
identity, not through an independently supplied equation `H v = 0`.

This file specializes the generic Noether calculus to the displayed augmented
Candidate-A operator.  It proves that every direction whose first variation
vanishes on a germ is annihilated by the actual H12 operator.  Finite families
of residual gauge, stabilizer, modulus or boundary symmetry directions can
therefore be attached before the no-hidden-mode/Gårding argument.
-/

